<title>EGYPT: Hoechst Orient net doubles in 1996.</title>
<headline>Hoechst Orient net doubles in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for calendar 1996:</p>
<p>(Egyptian pounds)</p>
<p>					1996		 1995</p>
<p>Net sales			166,218,690    154,092,190</p>
<p>Production costs	     124,325,193    125,450,948</p>
<p>Overheads			 31,382,150     23,971,762</p>
<p>Provisions			 6,080,030	1,969,089</p>
<p>Depreciation		     3,133,813	2,515,232</p>
<p>Net profit			 2,821,797	1,312,735</p>
<p>Full company name is Hoechst Orient, the Egyptian subsidiary of German firm Hoechst AG which owns a majority stake in the firm.</p>
<p>$1 =3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
